      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Thank you for the report, @{6a6bccb812d9cf9762d73225|full_name}!\n\nThis issue depends on the avatar and the world - for example, if an avatar consists of different meshes with different bounding boxes, some parts of the avatar may be occluded before others.\n\nThis can occur more frequently in worlds that use aggressive occlusion culling, i.e., near geometry that is not fully opaque, but configured as a large occluder.\n\nCulling issues are something that VRChat *should* address, but that would likely require more than just changing the camera settings.\n\nPerhaps VRChat could make it easier for avatar creators to discover culling issues before they occur, e.g., in the SDK. Please feel free to submit any suggestions as a separate feature request!",
